  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl, mix the cabbage, carrot, sweet onion, green onions, and dill pickle.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl, whisk together the mayonnaise, buttermilk, dill pickle juice, vinegar, mustard, sugar, cayenne pepper, and 3/4 teaspoon salt. Mash together the remaining salt and garlic, and whisk into the dressing. Drizzle dressing over the slaw, and toss to coat. Cover and refrigerate 8 hours, or overnight, before serving.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I didn't have a pickle, so I used a tablespoon of dill relish instead.  I also decreased sugar to 1/4 cup. It tasted great and got better with age."
    },
    {
      "text": "I substituted the dill pickle and pickle juice for sweet relish--just a personal preference. I add only a medium onion per head of cabbage. I have used sweet and spicy and Dijon mustards, all with great results. The sugar balances it out nicely."
    }
  ],
